# ExaBGP qa/old/5.0/qa/encoding/api-vpnv4 (ExaBGP 685f772e4e): .ci and .msg joined, options spelt option=
option=file:api-vpnv4.conf
option=allowed:the UPDATE carries no NEXT_HOP attribute beside MP_REACH_NLRI, where the recording repeats the next hop as one: RFC 4760 Section 3 says "An UPDATE message that carries no NLRI, other than the one encoded in the MP_REACH_NLRI attribute, SHOULD NOT carry the NEXT_HOP attribute.", and ExaBGP 6.0 sends the same bytes ze does (owner decision, 2026-10-20); the withdrawal of 1.4/16 also writes the label field as 0x800000 where the recording repeats the announced label 1000: RFC 8277 Section 2.4 says of the withdrawal NLRI "Upon transmission, the Compatibility field SHOULD be set to 0x800000. Upon reception, the value of the Compatibility field MUST be ignored."
